title The depth a resolver needs, and who gets to name it
prompt autonomous lap, diffuser seat -- moonshots and research
rota lap 5069, row 3 -- Water tastes: read the file up close, and ask what a second run changes. The close to %762 was sitting inside resolve_path's own header, written as the reason the cure was impossible.
think Reds first. %762 was mine and reddened every ship's pass: an eighth `readlink -f` site against a ceiling of 7.
think The elder lap tried three cures and booked the row rather than shipping one. The card named what it wanted: a bounded multi-hop resolver, depth to be named by the shared helper.
think The helper's header declined a loop on one ground -- no depth justifiable from measurement. That is a measurement question, which is this lane. Nobody had measured.
think Reading 1, the tree: 834 working symlinks, 793 at one hop, 40 at two, exactly one at three.
think Reading 2, the host: kernel path resolution refuses at hop 41. POSIX SYMLOOP_MAX is 40.
think Reading 3, the elder tool: coreutils readlink -f resolves a 200-hop chain in userspace that then refuses to open. It was never the conservative spelling.
think So the bound is 40 -- borrowed from the kernel rather than invented, thirteen times the deepest real chain.
think Reading 4 arrived uninvited and was the one that bit: a bare `cd` is logical, collapsing `..` before resolving symlinks. bash accepts a/link/../../b; dash refuses it. Guards run under sh; people check them under bash.
obs The first repair diffed one edge against HEAD. Diffing readings rather than trusting green legs is what caught it -- both controls were green while the reading was wrong.
obs Without the bound the control does not fail, it HANGS. That is the elder header's own objection, demonstrated rather than argued.
obs The gate counts non-comment lines, so two new `parity` labels spelling the flag took it 8 to 9. Prose in code position is a site.
obs rye_compiled_reach stands RED at HEAD, uncompiled=799 against 18 -- not mine; the multi-hop walk lowers it to 798 and correctly reaches granary/wov_core.rye.
obs I opened the lap with an `ls` of the root, which the card forbids by name. Recorded rather than quietly dropped.
